A||||7||88formula||Porting the exhaust manifolds ||||1||
Z||000000||88formula||04-03-2000||08:38 PM||||I have my manifolds off because of leaking gaskets, all the @#$%^&* bolt were lose. Anyway I want to port the restrictions in the manifolds out with a grinder. I have read that one should have the manifolds welded to strengthen the ported out area. MY question is why, from looking at them it doesn’t look like it would need it? If someone who has done this here recommends this with a good reason then were should they be welded?<P>Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||04-03-2000||08:43 PM||||Can you port the restrictions with a grinder? Thought only a dremmel could do this job? My guess is welding beads around the base will give you the extra insurance that it won't eventually crack there.||||reg||5
Z||000002||SCCA FIERO||04-03-2000||09:18 PM||||You only need to weld the part where the feet attatch to the head. You only need to do this if you are porting that part, not the restrictions down inside. If you hold the gasket up to the ports you can see how much can come off. The stock manifolds are welded right there where you would be grinding and when you open them up there, you end up grinding the weld completetly away. If you do get them welded <B>make sure the manifolds are bolted and torqued to a spare head to prevent warpage</B>||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||04-03-2000||09:20 PM||||This is what I read before I did mine.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/exhaust-manifolds.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/MotorCity/Garage/5007/fiero_osg/exhaust-manifolds.html</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000004||Eric||04-03-2000||09:41 PM||||If you take a look at the inside of the manifolds, you'll notice that the largest restriction is not at the flange but where the two pipes are welded to the main pipe.  If you want to be carefull and not warp the base, start with grinding the lower restrictions and leave the top alone.  No welds, nothing just grinding.  That metal is tough so get some good carbide bits.  I don't think you really need to go hog wild on these things.  After all, that's what headers are for.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||04-03-2000||10:54 PM||||Headers are $500 this is $30 max(for welding)  and the HP gain is almost the same.||||reg||1
Z||000006||DXR_DAD||04-03-2000||11:25 PM||||That's what I said..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||88formula||04-04-2000||06:20 PM||||Thanks for your replies.||||reg||1
